Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: latch NO_TIMESTAMP after qTimestamp fails

UFS 4.0 parts in the AYN Odin 3 reject QUERY_ATTR_IDN_TIMESTAMP
(Query RSP 0xfd → -EINVAL). ufshcd_set_timestamp_attr() is retried on
every runtime resume, about every 5–10 s, while holding the device
management lock.

That collides with ufshcd_devfreq_scale and jbd2: Steam's first
session (CEF + squashfuse + logs) then wedges the journal, steamwebhelper
sticks in D, SteamEngineWatch ptraces the client, and gamescope shows a
black Big Picture window.

If the attribute is unsupported once, never send it again.

Signed-off-by: lukemotion <darkplace@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -9137,9 +9137,15 @@
 
 	err = ufshcd_exec_dev_cmd(hba, DEV_CMD_TYPE_QUERY, dev_cmd_timeout);
 
-	if (err)
+	if (err) {
 		dev_err(hba->dev, "%s: failed to set timestamp %d\n",
 			__func__, err);
+		/*
+		 * Some UFS 4.0 devices advertise wspecversion >= 0x400 but
+		 * reject qTimestamp. Stop retrying on every runtime resume.
+		 */
+		hba->dev_quirks |= UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT;
+	}
 
 	ufshcd_dev_man_unlock(hba);
 }
